   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6. Handle Timestamp Gaps\n",
    "\n",
    "### Concept: Gap-Aware Rolling Features\n",
    "\n",
    "Our data has:\n",
    "- **Repeated timestamps** (0-second intervals)\n",
    "- **Normal intervals** (~2 seconds)\n",
    "- **Large gaps** (minutes to hours) where the logger was stopped\n",
    "\n",
    "If we compute rolling features across a large gap, we mix readings from different time periods. This creates misleading statistics.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Solution: Reset Rolling Windows After Large Gaps\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Compute time difference between consecutive rows: `timestamp.diff()`\n",
    "2. Identify gaps > 10 seconds\n",
    "3. Create a \"session\" identifier that increments after each large gap\n",
    "4. Compute rolling features **within each session** (groupby session)\n",
    "\n",
    "This way, rolling statistics never cross a recording interruption."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 5,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "output_type": "stream",
     "name": "stdout",
